# Pairs with RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog. A leaf recovery re-creates gets no fresh
# Zero block pin, so the GC, which no longer sees the retired entry, trims past
# writes the re-created leaf has not yet checkpointed. The base seeds the block
# pin on re-create (SetTreeIdAsync); the #4433 confirmation pass found its
# absence in the model.
MODULE: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLogRecreateSeedsNoBlockPin
TARGET: RecoveryNeverFallsOffLog
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a re-created leaf is not given a fresh block pin
PERTURBS: Recover

--- FIND
            /\ pinHlc' = [pinHlc EXCEPT ![l] = "zero"]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the retired entry is left in place.
            /\ pinHlc' = pinHlc
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot or a leaf row.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row and the snapshot both vanish: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END